# Applicable Functions and Levels Scope
<<DOC_CONTROL>>
> The upstream that bounds the register — which functions and which levels are required to carry objectives (per clause 6.2 ''at relevant functions and levels''); any explicit exclusions
## What this template gives you
This template helps you clearly define which parts of your organization are responsible for meeting specific objectives, and highlights any areas that are not included in your compliance program.
## When to use it
Use this document whenever you need to clarify which functions and levels are covered by your compliance objectives, and update it whenever there are changes to your organizational structure or responsibilities.
## Prerequisites
<<PREREQUISITES>>
## Cross-references
<<CROSS_REFERENCES>>
## Estimated effort
Expect to spend about 30 to 45 minutes completing this from scratch, as you''ll need to identify and describe each relevant function and level, plus any exclusions.
## 1. Functions in scope enumerated (engineering, ops, sales, legal, HR, finance as relevant)
<<MUST item:6.2:scope_functions>>
_Why: Clause 6.2 — relevant functions_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 2. Levels in scope enumerated (org / business unit / function / team)
<<MUST item:6.2:scope_levels>>
_Why: Clause 6.2 — relevant levels_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 3. Exclusions stated explicitly with rationale
<<MUST item:6.2:scope_exclusions>>
_Why: Defensible bounding_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## Recommended additions
_The items below strengthen the artefact but are not strictly required for the MUST checks. Fill in any that apply to your environment._
### 1. Cascade rules (how org objectives cascade into BU/function objectives)
<<SHOULD item:6.2:scope_cascade>>
_Why: Coherence_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## Revision history
<<REVISION_HISTORY>>
', 'req__6_2__applicable_functions_scope.md', 3, 1, '2026-08-09 12:24:34.699322+00', 'load_to_postgres.py');
