INSERT INTO public.templates (leaf_id, template_version, body_md, source_file, must_count, should_count, last_loaded_at, last_loaded_by) VALUES ('req:A.7.3.5:objection_procedure', 1, '---
leaf_id: req:A.7.3.5:objection_procedure
control_ref: A.7.3.5
standard_id: ISO27701:2019
evidence_type: procedure
trigger_type: profile_fact
template_version: 1
must_count: 5
should_count: 1
# Objection Handling Procedure
<<DOC_CONTROL>>
> §7.3.5 requires an objection mechanism. Two flavours: absolute (Art.21.2 direct marketing / Art.21.6 statistics) and balancing-test (Art.21.1 legitimate-interests processing). Companion procedure to A.7.2.2 lawful basis.
## What this template gives you
This template helps you document how your organization handles objections from individuals regarding the use of their personal data, including direct marketing and legitimate interest scenarios. It ensures you meet privacy compliance requirements under ISO 27701.
## When to use it
Use this procedure whenever someone objects to your processing of their personal data, such as for marketing or statistical purposes. Review and update the document as needed, especially if your data processing activities or legal obligations change.
## Prerequisites
<<PREREQUISITES>>
## Cross-references
<<CROSS_REFERENCES>>
## Estimated effort
Expect to spend about 50 to 75 minutes completing this template from scratch, as it requires you to address five key elements in detail.
## 1. Channel consistency with service type (online services offer online objection; §7.3.5 implementation guidance)
<<MUST item:A.7.3.5:proc_channel_consistency>>
_Why: §7.3.5 — consistent with service type_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 2. Absolute objection handling (Art.21.2 marketing → processing must stop immediately)
<<MUST item:A.7.3.5:proc_absolute_objection>>
_Why: GDPR Art.21.2-3_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 3. Legitimate-interests balancing test — org demonstrates compelling grounds override subject rights or objection prevails
<<MUST item:A.7.3.5:proc_balancing_test>>
_Why: GDPR Art.21.1_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 4. Information provision — subjects informed of objection right at first communication (Art.21.4)
<<MUST item:A.7.3.5:proc_information_provision>>
_Why: GDPR Art.21.4_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 5. Response-time SLA stated + honoured
<<MUST item:A.7.3.5:proc_response_sla>>
_Why: §7.3.5 implementation_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## Recommended additions
_The items below strengthen the artefact but are not strictly required for the MUST checks. Fill in any that apply to your environment._
### 1. Named owner (DPO + Marketing lead for A.21.2 cases)
<<SHOULD item:A.7.3.5:proc_owner>>
_Why: Accountability_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## Revision history
<<REVISION_HISTORY>>
', 'req__A_7_3_5__objection_procedure.md', 5, 1, '2026-08-09 12:24:34.699322+00', 'load_to_postgres.py');
