INSERT INTO public.templates (leaf_id, template_version, body_md, source_file, must_count, should_count, last_loaded_at, last_loaded_by) VALUES ('req:A.7.3.8:copy_provision_procedure', 1, '---
leaf_id: req:A.7.3.8:copy_provision_procedure
control_ref: A.7.3.8
standard_id: ISO27701:2019
evidence_type: procedure
trigger_type: profile_fact
template_version: 1
must_count: 6
should_count: 1
# PII Copy Provision Procedure
<<DOC_CONTROL>>
> §7.3.8 requires the org to provide a copy of processed PII on request. Bridges to Art.15.3 (copy of PII) + Art.20 (portability — structured, commonly used, machine-readable format).
## What this template gives you
This template helps you create a clear procedure for providing individuals with a copy of their personal data upon request, ensuring compliance with privacy regulations and supporting data portability requirements.
## When to use it
Use this procedure whenever someone requests a copy of their personal information your organization processes. Update the document as needed, especially if your data handling practices or legal requirements change.
## Prerequisites
<<PREREQUISITES>>
## Cross-references
<<CROSS_REFERENCES>>
## Estimated effort
Expect to spend about 60 to 90 minutes drafting this procedure from scratch, as each of the six required elements will take around 10 to 15 minutes to complete.
## 1. Format selection — structured, commonly used, accessible (Art.15.3 + machine-readable for Art.20)
<<MUST item:A.7.3.8:proc_format_selection>>
_Why: §7.3.8 — structured, commonly used format_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 2. Scope restriction — copy relates specifically to that subject; no cross-subject leakage
<<MUST item:A.7.3.8:proc_scope_restriction>>
_Why: §7.3.8 — relate specifically to that PII principal_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 3. Deleted-PII notification — where PII already deleted per retention policy, subject informed of that fact
<<MUST item:A.7.3.8:proc_deleted_notification>>
_Why: §7.3.8 — inform PII principal that PII has been deleted_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 4. No-re-identification rule — de-identified data not re-identified solely to fulfil this control
<<MUST item:A.7.3.8:proc_no_reidentification>>
_Why: §7.3.8 — should not seek to (re-)identify_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 5. Direct-transfer capability — where technically feasible, transfer directly to another controller (Art.20.2)
<<MUST item:A.7.3.8:proc_direct_transfer>>
_Why: §7.3.8 — transfer copy from one organization to another_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 6. Response-time SLA stated + honoured
<<MUST item:A.7.3.8:proc_response_sla>>
_Why: Art.12.3_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## Recommended additions
_The items below strengthen the artefact but are not strictly required for the MUST checks. Fill in any that apply to your environment._
### 1. Self-service export where feasible
<<SHOULD item:A.7.3.8:proc_self_service>>
_Why: Efficiency_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## Revision history
<<REVISION_HISTORY>>
', 'req__A_7_3_8__copy_provision_procedure.md', 6, 1, '2026-08-09 12:24:34.699322+00', 'load_to_postgres.py');
INSERT INTO public.templates (leaf_id, template_version, body_md, source_file, must_count, should_count, last_loaded_at, last_loaded_by) VALUES ('req:8.3:operational_risk_treatment_record', 1, '---
leaf_id: req:8.3:operational_risk_treatment_record
