# PII Accuracy + Quality Procedure
<<DOC_CONTROL>>
> §7.4.3 requires the org to maintain PII accuracy + completeness + currency throughout the lifecycle. Bridges to GDPR Art.5.1.d accuracy + Art.16 rectification. Cross-links to A.7.3.6 correction procedure.
## What this template gives you
This template helps you create a clear procedure for keeping personal information accurate, complete, and up to date, supporting both ISO 27701 and GDPR requirements. It''s useful if you need to show how you manage and correct personal data.
## When to use it
Use this template whenever your organization needs to document how it maintains and updates personal information, especially if your activities match certain triggers. Review and update the procedure as needed to stay current.
## Prerequisites
<<PREREQUISITES>>
## Cross-references
<<CROSS_REFERENCES>>
## Estimated effort
Expect to spend about 50 to 75 minutes to complete this template from scratch, as each required section takes around 10 to 15 minutes to write.
## 1. Inaccuracy prevention — technical + procedural controls (input validation + duplicate detection + integration reconciliation)
<<MUST item:A.7.4.3:proc_inaccuracy_prevention>>
_Why: §7.4.3 — minimize inaccuracies_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 2. Inaccuracy response — how the org responds when inaccuracy is detected (internal + subject-flagged)
<<MUST item:A.7.4.3:proc_inaccuracy_response>>
_Why: §7.4.3 — respond to inaccurate PII_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 3. Lifecycle coverage — applies at collection + processing + storage + sharing + disposal stages
<<MUST item:A.7.4.3:proc_lifecycle_coverage>>
_Why: §7.4.3 — throughout the lifecycle_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 4. Cross-link to A.7.3.6 correction procedure — subject-initiated rectification handled there
<<MUST item:A.7.4.3:proc_correction_link>>
_Why: Integration_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 5. Up-to-date check cadence per PII category (e.g. contact details refresh cadence)
<<MUST item:A.7.4.3:proc_up_to_date_check>>
_Why: §7.4.3 — up-to-date_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## Recommended additions
_The items below strengthen the artefact but are not strictly required for the MUST checks. Fill in any that apply to your environment._
### 1. Named owner (Data Ops + Privacy Engineering)
<<SHOULD item:A.7.4.3:proc_owner>>
_Why: Accountability_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## Revision history
<<REVISION_HISTORY>>
', 'req__A_7_4_3__accuracy_procedure.md', 5, 1, '2026-08-09 12:24:34.699322+00', 'load_to_postgres.py');
