# ISMS Manual / Charter
<<DOC_CONTROL>>
> Clause 4.4 requires the organisation to establish, implement, maintain, and continually improve an ISMS including its processes and their interactions. The ISMS manual is the canonical artefact describing the system as a whole. Sibling leaves: process interaction map, per-update change record, program review
## What this template gives you
This template helps you create a comprehensive manual that describes your Information Security Management System (ISMS) and how its processes work together. It''s useful for showing how your security program is structured and maintained.
## When to use it
Use this template whenever you need to document or update your ISMS, as it should always reflect your current environment. Refresh the manual as needed to keep it accurate and up to date.
## Prerequisites
<<PREREQUISITES>>
## Cross-references
<<CROSS_REFERENCES>>
## Estimated effort
Expect to spend about 60 to 90 minutes drafting this document from scratch, since there are several required elements to cover in detail.
## 1. Reference to ISMS scope statement (4.3)
<<MUST item:4.4:scope_ref>>
_Why: Clause 4.4 — establish_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 2. ISMS processes enumerated (planning, operation, evaluation, improvement)
<<MUST item:4.4:processes>>
_Why: Clause 4.4 — processes needed_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 3. Interactions between processes described (inputs, outputs, sequence)
<<MUST item:4.4:interactions>>
_Why: Clause 4.4 — their interactions_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 4. Governance structure (ownership, decision rights, escalation)
<<MUST item:4.4:governance>>
_Why: Clause 4.4 — maintain_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 5. Continual improvement statement and mechanism
<<MUST item:4.4:improvement_intent>>
_Why: Clause 4.4 — continually improve_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 6. Named owner of the manual (ISMS Manager)
<<MUST item:4.4:owner>>
_Why: Accountability_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## Recommended additions
_The items below strengthen the artefact but are not strictly required for the MUST checks. Fill in any that apply to your environment._
### 1. References ISO 27001:2022 clause structure (auditor navigation)
<<SHOULD item:4.4:references_iso>>
_Why: Auditor navigation_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## Revision history
<<REVISION_HISTORY>>
', 'req__4_4__isms_manual.md', 6, 1, '2026-08-09 12:24:34.699322+00', 'load_to_postgres.py');
