This template helps you set clear rules for working in secure areas, including who can enter, what devices are allowed, and how to keep records of work sessions. It''s designed to help you meet ISO 27001 requirements for physical security.
## When to use it
Use this procedure whenever your organization has areas that need extra security controls, such as server rooms or restricted offices. Review and update it whenever your secure areas or security practices change.
## Prerequisites
<<PREREQUISITES>>
## Cross-references
<<CROSS_REFERENCES>>
## Estimated effort
Expect to spend about 60 to 90 minutes drafting this procedure from scratch, depending on the number of secure areas and how many details you need to document.
## 1. Secure area definition (which areas are ''secure'' per A.7.1 classification)
<<MUST item:A.7.6:secure_area_definition>>
_Why: 27002:7.6 — secure areas_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 2. Restrictions on personal devices, recording, photography
<<MUST item:A.7.6:device_restrictions>>
_Why: 27002:7.6 — security measures_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
