# Applicable Art.27 Scope
<<DOC_CONTROL>>
> The upstream — whether the controller/processor is in scope for Art.27 (not established in EU AND processing falls under Art.3.2) and any Art.27.2 exceptions (occasional + no large-scale special-category + low risk + public authority)
## What this template gives you
This template helps you determine if your organization needs to appoint an EU representative under GDPR Article 27, and whether any exceptions apply to your situation.
## When to use it
Use this document when your business is not established in the EU but processes personal data of people in the EU, and review it whenever your processing activities or business profile change.
## Prerequisites
<<PREREQUISITES>>
## Cross-references
<<CROSS_REFERENCES>>
## Estimated effort
Expect to spend about 30 to 45 minutes completing this from scratch, as you''ll need to address three required elements and review your data processing activities carefully.
## 1. Establishment analysis — where the controller/processor is established + why Art.3.2 applies (offering goods/services OR monitoring behaviour in Union)
<<MUST item:Art.27:scope_establishment>>
_Why: Art.3.2_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 2. MS targeted (Art.27.3 — representative MUST be in one of these)
<<MUST item:Art.27:scope_member_state_target>>
_Why: Art.27.3_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 3. Art.27.2 exception assessment (occasional processing + no special-category-large-scale + low risk → no representative needed). Decision recorded
<<MUST item:Art.27:scope_art27_2_exception>>
_Why: Art.27.2_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## Recommended additions
_The items below strengthen the artefact but are not strictly required for the MUST checks. Fill in any that apply to your environment._
### 1. Trigger list (EU market entry/exit, processing-pattern change)
<<SHOULD item:Art.27:scope_change_drivers>>
_Why: Currency_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## Revision history
<<REVISION_HISTORY>>
', 'req__Art_27__applicable_scope.md', 3, 1, '2026-08-09 12:24:34.699322+00', 'load_to_postgres.py');
