| Reg Finding Id | Reg Asset | Reg Severity | Reg Sla Due | Reg Status | Reg Sla Breaches |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
|          |          |          |          |          |          |
|          |          |          |          |          |          |
|          |          |          |          |          |          |
<!-- EDIT-ZONE-END leaf:req:A.8.8:vulnerability_backlog_register -->
## Column guidance — what to fill in
### Reg Finding Id
<<MUST item:A.8.8:reg_finding_id>>
_Why: Auditability_
> _Standard text:_ Per-finding unique identifier (CVE / vendor advisory / scanner finding ref)
<<GUIDANCE>>
### Reg Asset
<<MUST item:A.8.8:reg_asset>>
_Why: Cross-control coherence_
> _Standard text:_ Per-finding affected asset (from A.5.9 register)
<<GUIDANCE>>
### Reg Severity
<<MUST item:A.8.8:reg_severity>>
_Why: 27002:8.8 — evaluated_
> _Standard text:_ Per-finding triaged severity (from procedure rubric, not raw CVSS)
<<GUIDANCE>>
### Reg Sla Due
<<MUST item:A.8.8:reg_sla_due>>
_Why: Drives action_
> _Standard text:_ Per-finding SLA due date (derived from severity + first-seen date)
<<GUIDANCE>>
### Reg Status
<<MUST item:A.8.8:reg_status>>
_Why: Continuous evidence_
> _Standard text:_ Per-finding status (open / mitigated / patched / accepted-with-expiry)
<<GUIDANCE>>
### Reg Sla Breaches
<<MUST item:A.8.8:reg_sla_breaches>>
_Why: Auditor-critical defensibility_
> _Standard text:_ SLA-breach flag per row + escalation evidence where breached
<<GUIDANCE>>
## Recommended additional columns
_These columns strengthen the register but are not strictly required for the MUST checks. Add them to the table if they apply to your environment._
### Reg Dashboard
