# Automated Decision Subject Obligations Procedure
<<DOC_CONTROL>>
> §7.3.10 requires the org to identify + address obligations to subjects arising from solely-automated decisions producing legal or similarly significant effects. Companion to the already-curated GDPR Art.22 4-leaf (this is the 27701-side counterpart).
## What this template gives you
This template helps you document how your organization handles obligations to individuals affected by decisions made entirely by automated systems, especially when those decisions have significant legal or similar impacts.
## When to use it
Use this procedure whenever your organization makes important decisions about people using only automated processes, and update it whenever your practices or systems change in ways that affect these obligations.
## Prerequisites
<<PREREQUISITES>>
## Cross-references
<<CROSS_REFERENCES>>
## Estimated effort
Expect to spend about 60 to 90 minutes completing this template from scratch, as it covers six required elements and one recommended section.
## 1. Notification-of-existence — subjects informed that automated decision-making occurs (Art.13.2.f + 14.2.g)
<<MUST item:A.7.3.10:proc_notification_of_existence>>
_Why: §7.3.10 — notifying the existence_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 2. Meaningful information about the logic + envisaged consequences
<<MUST item:A.7.3.10:proc_meaningful_logic>>
_Why: GDPR Art.13.2.f + Art.15.1.h_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 3. Objection pathway — subjects can object to automated decision-making
<<MUST item:A.7.3.10:proc_objection_pathway>>
_Why: §7.3.10 — allow objection_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 4. Human intervention pathway (Art.22.3)
<<MUST item:A.7.3.10:proc_human_intervention>>
_Why: §7.3.10 — human intervention + Art.22.3_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 5. Jurisdiction-specific full-automation prohibition awareness (§7.3.10 NOTE — some jurisdictions restrict full automation)
<<MUST item:A.7.3.10:proc_jurisdiction_prohibition>>
_Why: §7.3.10 NOTE_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 6. Cross-link to A.7.2.5 PIA and the Art.22 4-leaf procedure register — no double-registration; this control handles the SUBJECT-facing obligations while Art.22 procedure handles the internal governance
<<MUST item:A.7.3.10:proc_cross_link_art22>>
_Why: GDPR Art.22 alignment_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## Recommended additions
_The items below strengthen the artefact but are not strictly required for the MUST checks. Fill in any that apply to your environment._
### 1. Named owner (DPO + ML/Product lead)
<<SHOULD item:A.7.3.10:proc_owner>>
_Why: Accountability_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## Revision history
<<REVISION_HISTORY>>
', 'req__A_7_3_10__automated_decision_obligations_procedure.md', 6, 1, '2026-08-09 12:24:34.699322+00', 'load_to_postgres.py');
