# Privacy Notice Delivery Procedure
<<DOC_CONTROL>>
> §7.3.3 governs HOW subjects actually receive + access the notice content determined in §7.3.2 — timely, concise, complete, transparent, intelligible, easily accessible + in clear plain language.
## What this template gives you
This template helps you document how you deliver privacy notices to individuals, ensuring the information is clear, accessible, and meets regulatory expectations for transparency and plain language.
## When to use it
Use this procedure whenever your organization needs to provide privacy notices to people, especially when your activities match certain criteria. Update the document whenever there are changes in how notices are delivered.
## Prerequisites
<<PREREQUISITES>>
## Cross-references
<<CROSS_REFERENCES>>
## Estimated effort
Expect to spend about 50 to 75 minutes preparing this from scratch, as each required section takes roughly 10 to 15 minutes to complete.
## 1. At-collection delivery — notice presented when PII is collected (form, signup flow, kiosk)
<<MUST item:A.7.3.3:proc_at_collection>>
_Why: §7.3.3 — given at time of PII collection_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 2. Permanent accessibility — notice available at stable URL / in-product location at any time
<<MUST item:A.7.3.3:proc_permanent_access>>
_Why: §7.3.3 — permanently accessible_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 3. Plain-language standard — reading-level target, jargon audit, tested against target audience
<<MUST item:A.7.3.3:proc_plain_language>>
_Why: §7.3.3 — clear and plain language_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 4. Layered / progressive design (short summary + expandable detail) where notice is long
<<MUST item:A.7.3.3:proc_layered_design>>
_Why: §7.3.3 — concise + easily accessible_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 5. Visual aids where helpful (icons, diagrams — per §7.3.3 NOTE)
<<MUST item:A.7.3.3:proc_visual_aids>>
_Why: §7.3.3 NOTE — icons and images_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## Recommended additions
_The items below strengthen the artefact but are not strictly required for the MUST checks. Fill in any that apply to your environment._
### 1. Readability target stated (Flesch score / school-grade)
<<SHOULD item:A.7.3.3:proc_readability_target>>
_Why: Measurable clarity_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## Revision history
<<REVISION_HISTORY>>
', 'req__A_7_3_3__notice_delivery_procedure.md', 5, 1, '2026-08-09 12:24:34.699322+00', 'load_to_postgres.py');
