# ISMS Risk and Opportunity Planning Procedure
<<DOC_CONTROL>>
> Clause 6.1.1 requires the organisation to consider 4.1 issues + 4.2 requirements and determine risks and opportunities. The procedure is the canonical artefact linking inputs to actions. Sibling leaves: action register, applicable inputs scope, program review
## What this template gives you
This template helps you document how your organization identifies and manages risks and opportunities related to your information security management system. It connects your business context and stakeholder needs to practical actions.
## When to use it
Use this procedure whenever you need to show how your organization considers internal and external issues, as well as stakeholder requirements, to address risks and opportunities. Review and update it whenever significant changes occur.
## Prerequisites
<<PREREQUISITES>>
## Cross-references
<<CROSS_REFERENCES>>
## Estimated effort
Expect to spend about 1.5 to 2 hours completing this from scratch, as each required section takes some time to fill in with details specific to your organization.
## 1. Issues from 4.1 considered as planning input
<<MUST item:6.1.1:issues_input>>
_Why: Clause 6.1.1 — issues referred to in 4.1_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 2. Requirements from 4.2 considered as planning input
<<MUST item:6.1.1:requirements_input>>
_Why: Clause 6.1.1 — requirements referred to in 4.2_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 3. Risks identified that need to be addressed for ISMS to achieve intended outcomes
<<MUST item:6.1.1:risks_identified>>
_Why: Clause 6.1.1 — risks that need to be addressed_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 4. Opportunities identified to enhance ISMS effectiveness
<<MUST item:6.1.1:opportunities>>
_Why: Clause 6.1.1 — opportunities_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 5. Actions planned to address risks and opportunities
<<MUST item:6.1.1:actions_planned>>
_Why: Clause 6.1.1 — actions to address_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 6. Integration of planned actions into ISMS processes
<<MUST item:6.1.1:integration>>
_Why: Clause 6.1.1 — integrated into ISMS processes_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 7. Evaluation of effectiveness of planned actions
<<MUST item:6.1.1:evaluation>>
_Why: Clause 6.1.1 — evaluate effectiveness_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## Recommended additions
_The items below strengthen the artefact but are not strictly required for the MUST checks. Fill in any that apply to your environment._
### 1. Link to risk assessment process (6.1.2)
<<SHOULD item:6.1.1:risk_assessment_link>>
_Why: Closes the planning loop_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
