# Nonconformity and Corrective Action Procedure
<<DOC_CONTROL>>
> Clause 10.2 requires the organisation to react to nonconformity, evaluate causes, implement corrective action, review effectiveness, and update the ISMS if needed. The procedure is the canonical artefact. Sibling leaves: NC register (per-NC lifecycle), applicable NC sources scope, program review
## What this template gives you
This template helps you document how your organization identifies, investigates, and addresses problems or failures in your information security management system. It guides you through taking corrective action and keeping records for compliance with ISO 27001.
## When to use it
Use this procedure whenever a security issue or nonconformity is found in your environment, and update it as needed to reflect changes or improvements in your processes.
## Prerequisites
<<PREREQUISITES>>
## Cross-references
<<CROSS_REFERENCES>>
## Estimated effort
Expect to spend about 60 to 90 minutes drafting this procedure from scratch, depending on the complexity of your environment and the number of nonconformities you need to address.
## 1. React to the nonconformity — control, correct, and deal with consequences
<<MUST item:10.2:react>>
_Why: Clause 10.2 a)_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 2. Evaluate the need for action to eliminate causes (root cause analysis)
<<MUST item:10.2:root_cause>>
_Why: Clause 10.2 b)_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 3. Implement corrective action
<<MUST item:10.2:implementation>>
_Why: Clause 10.2 c)_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 4. Review effectiveness of corrective action taken
<<MUST item:10.2:effectiveness>>
_Why: Clause 10.2 d)_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 5. Make changes to the ISMS where appropriate
<<MUST item:10.2:isms_update>>
_Why: Clause 10.2 e)_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 6. Documented information retained on the nature of NC, actions taken, and results
<<MUST item:10.2:document>>
_Why: Clause 10.2 — documented information_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## Recommended additions
_The items below strengthen the artefact but are not strictly required for the MUST checks. Fill in any that apply to your environment._
### 1. Link to A.5.26 (incident response) and A.5.27 (lessons learned)
<<SHOULD item:10.2:incident_link>>
_Why: Operational coherence_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## Revision history
<<REVISION_HISTORY>>
', 'req__10_2__nonconformity_corrective_action.md', 6, 1, '2026-08-09 12:24:34.699322+00', 'load_to_postgres.py');
