# Applicable Information-Society Services Scope
<<DOC_CONTROL>>
> The upstream — which services count as ''offered directly to a child'' under Art.8. Critical for B2B / professional-service tenants who may incidentally process minors'' data but don''t ''offer to'' them directly (e.g. a parent purchases on a family-account UI)
## What this template gives you
This template helps you clarify whether your services are considered ''offered directly to a child'' under GDPR Article 8, especially if you provide B2B or professional services that might incidentally involve minors'' data.
## When to use it
Use this document whenever your business activities could match scenarios where minors'' data is processed, such as when a parent uses your service on behalf of a child. Update it as your service offerings or user profiles change.
## Prerequisites
<<PREREQUISITES>>
## Cross-references
<<CROSS_REFERENCES>>
## Estimated effort
Expect to spend about 30 to 45 minutes completing this from scratch, as you''ll need to address three required elements and possibly one recommended section.
## 1. Services in scope enumerated (those advertised to / used by minors directly)
<<MUST item:Art.8:scope_in_scope_services>>
_Why: Art.8.1 — offered directly_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 2. Incidental-minor-data scenarios stated (and why they don''t trigger Art.8 — e.g. parent account holder)
<<MUST item:Art.8:scope_incidental_processing>>
_Why: Defensibility_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 3. Member State age threshold variations (where org operates in multiple Member States)
<<MUST item:Art.8:scope_member_state_thresholds>>
_Why: Art.8.1 — Member State law_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## Recommended additions
_The items below strengthen the artefact but are not strictly required for the MUST checks. Fill in any that apply to your environment._
### 1. Trigger list for re-scoping (new product line touching minors, new Member State entry)
<<SHOULD item:Art.8:scope_change_drivers>>
_Why: Currency_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## Revision history
<<REVISION_HISTORY>>
', 'req__Art_8__applicable_services_scope.md', 3, 1, '2026-08-09 12:24:34.699322+00', 'load_to_postgres.py');
