# Right to Object Procedure
<<DOC_CONTROL>>
> Art.21 gives subjects the right to object to processing based on legitimate interests / public task (Art.21.1) AND an absolute right to object to direct marketing (Art.21.2). Distinct workflows for absolute (direct marketing) vs balancing (legitimate interests)
## What this template gives you
This template helps you create a clear procedure for handling individuals’ objections to your use of their personal data, including both direct marketing and other legitimate interests under GDPR.
## When to use it
Use this whenever you process personal data and need to address requests from people who object to your data use, especially for direct marketing or when balancing your interests against their rights. Update the procedure whenever your practices or legal requirements change.
## Prerequisites
<<PREREQUISITES>>
## Cross-references
<<CROSS_REFERENCES>>
## Estimated effort
Expect to spend about 60 to 90 minutes drafting this procedure from scratch, as you’ll need to cover several required elements to ensure full compliance.
## 1. Intake channel via Art.12 procedure
<<MUST item:Art.21:intake_channel>>
_Why: Art.12.2_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 2. Direct marketing objection — absolute right, immediate cessation (Art.21.3)
<<MUST item:Art.21:direct_marketing_absolute>>
_Why: Art.21.2-3_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 3. Legitimate-interests objection — balancing test (compelling legitimate grounds OR establishment of legal claims)
<<MUST item:Art.21:legitimate_interests_balance>>
_Why: Art.21.1_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 4. Right is explicitly drawn to subject''s attention at first communication (Art.21.4)
<<MUST item:Art.21:explicit_notice>>
_Why: Art.21.4 — explicit notice_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 5. One-month response deadline
<<MUST item:Art.21:response_deadline>>
_Why: Art.12.3_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 6. Scientific-research / statistical-purposes overlay (Art.21.6 — public-interest task derogation)
<<MUST item:Art.21:scientific_research>>
_Why: Art.21.6_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## Recommended additions
_The items below strengthen the artefact but are not strictly required for the MUST checks. Fill in any that apply to your environment._
### 1. Profiling objection handled explicitly (Art.21.1 covers profiling)
<<SHOULD item:Art.21:profiling_handling>>
