## What this template gives you
This template guides you through the process of conducting a Data Protection Impact Assessment (DPIA), ensuring you meet GDPR requirements when handling data processing that could pose high risks to individuals’ privacy.
## When to use it
Use this procedure whenever your planned data processing activities might result in a high risk to people’s rights and freedoms, or when specific triggers under GDPR apply. Review and update as needed if your processing activities or risks change.
## Prerequisites
<<PREREQUISITES>>
## Cross-references
<<CROSS_REFERENCES>>
## Estimated effort
Expect to spend about 60 to 90 minutes completing this template from scratch, as you’ll need to address six required elements and one recommended section.
## 1. Trigger criteria — Art.35.3 mandatory cases (systematic monitoring / special-category large-scale / public-area large-scale monitoring) PLUS SA-published list + sectoral guidance
<<MUST item:Art.35:trigger_criteria>>
_Why: Art.35.1 + Art.35.3-4_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 2. DPO advice mandatory (Art.35.2) — DPO consulted during DPIA, advice recorded
<<MUST item:Art.35:dpo_advice>>
_Why: Art.35.2_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 3. Minimum content per Art.35.7 (systematic description + necessity/proportionality + risks + measures to address)
<<MUST item:Art.35:content_minimum>>
_Why: Art.35.7_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 4. Subject consultation considered (Art.35.9) — where appropriate, views of subjects/representatives sought
<<MUST item:Art.35:subject_consultation>>
_Why: Art.35.9_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 5. Art.36 prior-consultation escalation — when residual high risk remains, escalate to SA
<<MUST item:Art.35:art36_escalation>>
_Why: Art.36.1_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## 6. Review trigger — DPIA reviewed when processing risk changes (Art.35.11)
<<MUST item:Art.35:review_trigger>>
_Why: Art.35.11_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## Recommended additions
_The items below strengthen the artefact but are not strictly required for the MUST checks. Fill in any that apply to your environment._
### 1. Named owner (DPO)
<<SHOULD item:Art.35:proc_owner>>
_Why: Accountability_
<<GUIDANCE>>
<<TEXT>>
## Revision history
<<REVISION_HISTORY>>
', 'req__Art_35__dpia_procedure.md', 6, 1, '2026-08-09 12:24:34.699322+00', 'load_to_postgres.py');
